ashed box highlights the top-left plot (DAE, Style Space). A black curved arrow points from this highlighted area to the right side of the image, accompanied by the text '(DAE shows a clearer separation than VAE in Style Space)'. Below the document snippet, the text 'Evidence Yelpr in the document' is visible. Above the document, the query is stated: 'Question: Which model's style space shows a clearer separation between different styles according to Figure 2?'.\n\nThe right side of the image lists the responses from four different AI models to the question, each marked with an emoji indicating correctness or error. \n1. 'GPT-4o-mini' is marked with a red 'X' emoji. Its response states: 'According to Figure 2, the VAE model's style space shows a clearer separation between different styles.'\n2. 'LightRAG' is marked with a red 'X' emoji. Its response states: 'According to Figure 2, the Variational Autoencoder (VAE) shows a clearer separation between different styles in its style space compared to the Deterministic Autoencoder (DAE).'\n3. 'MMGraphRAG' is marked with a red 'X' emoji. Its response states: 'According to Figure 2, the model's style space shows a clearer separation between different styles in the Variational Autoencoder (VAE) compared to the Deterministic Autoencoder (DAE).'\n4. 'RAG-Anything' is marked with a green checkmark emoji and the label '(Correct)'. Its response states: 'The DAE model's style space shows a clearer separation between different styles according to Figure 2.'\n\nThe visual layout contrasts the incorrect answers of the baseline models (GPT-4o-mini, LightRAG, MMGraphRAG), which all incorrectly identify the VAE model, with the correct answer provided by RAG-Anything, which correctly identifies the DAE model based on the visual evidence in the highlighted figure."}
